00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Bosko and Honey is a comedy, animation, music film directed by Hugh Harman.

2
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,000
This is an unreleased cartoon that eventually went on to have most
of its animation recycled by Bosko's Dizzy Date.

3
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Honey is trying to teach the violin to Wilbur, the one who hates music.

4
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Honey calls Bosko over.

5
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Bosko and Honey sing, dance, and play music while
Wilbur continues to express its disdain.

6
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Honey (voice) (uncredited), played by Rochelle Hudson.

7
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Bosko / Wilbur (voice) (uncredited), played by Johnny Murray.

8
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Bosko is an animated cartoon character created by
animators Hugh Harman and Rudolf Ising.

9
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Bosko was the first recurring character in Leon Schlesinger's cartoon series and
was the star of 39 Looney Tunes shorts released by Warner Bros.

10
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
He was voiced by Carman Maxwell, Bernard B.

11
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Brown, Johnny Murray, and Philip Hurlic during the 1920s and
1930s and once by Don Messick during the 1990s.

12
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
The film explores themes of music teacher, anthropomorphism, short film.

13
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:36,000
The tone is lighthearted.
